The bundled Kindle compatibility helper is separate third-party software:
KindleUnpack, commit bf0ca6ece4e73494625e7950be3e259b6260774c,
https://github.com/kevinhendricks/KindleUnpack, GPL-3.0. Its complete unmodified
library source and licence accompany each binary distribution in tools/kindle.
The HomeLibre wrapper is tools/kindle/convert_kf8.py. It invokes KindleUnpack
in a separate private Python process and does not alter the original book.

The private CPython 3.13.16 embedded runtime and its licence are included in
tools/kindle/python. No system Python installation is required. Exact download
URLs and checksums are recorded in Installer/KINDLE_RUNTIME.json in the source.

The separate DjVu page renderer uses the unmodified DjVuLibre 3.5.29 Windows
decoder library and command-line tools, GPL-2.0-or-later. Their complete matching source archive,
copyright notice and licence accompany the binaries in tools/djvu. HomeLibre
runs HomeLibDjvu as a private persistent process, passing finished pixels
directly to the reader. Its complete source is in tools/djvu/HomeLibDjvu-source
and Utils/HomeLibDjvu in the repository. It performs no OCR. The IJG JPEG, libtiff and zlib notices accompany their original DLLs.
Exact official download URLs and checksums are in Installer/RASTER_RUNTIME.json.

The private full 7-Zip 26.05 command-line decoder and DLL are included for RAR
comic archives. They are unmodified, with their original License.txt in
tools/7zip. This includes LGPL/BSD components and the unRAR restriction;
see that file and https://www.7-zip.org/license.txt for details.

The embedded dark VCL interface uses the unmodified Charcoal Dark Slate
redistributable style supplied with Embarcadero RAD Studio 13. This style is
separate from the MIT-licensed HomeLibre source code.

The separate binary Office reader uses DocSharp.Binary.Doc, Common, Ppt and Xls
0.21.0, by manfromarce, under the MIT licence. It includes code from
b2xtranslator under its BSD 3-Clause licence. Both licences accompany the
unmodified assemblies in tools/doc. The HomeLibDoc wrapper source is in
Utils/HomeLibDoc. Exact package URLs and checksums are recorded in
Installer/DOC_RUNTIME.json. It opens books read-only and writes the converted
document to a private cache.

WPS and WordPerfect use the unmodified libwps/libwpd/librevenge command-line
readers on 64-bit Windows (MPL-2.0). Their matching source packages, licenses,
MSYS2 clang64 runtime notices and package hashes accompany tools/office.
See Installer/OFFICE_LEGACY_RUNTIME.json and OfficeLegacy-NOTICE.txt.


The standalone legacy-book helper is separate GPL-3.0 software adapted from
calibre and DeDRM_tools. Its matching sources, source pins, native build script
and license notices are in tools/bookconvert and scripts/prepare-legacy-runtime.py
in the HomeLibre source repository. Distributions carry its Python sources,
GPL/LGPL notices and SOURCE.json beside the helper. LZX uses libmspack
(LGPL-2.1); the D3DES core is public domain, with OpenCLit substitution tables
(GPL-2.0-or-later). See tools/bookconvert/THIRD_PARTY.md for exact attribution.

The HA CPY/ASC decoder is an Apache-2.0 adaptation of unarc-rs; its pinned
source attribution and full license are in tools/bookconvert/vendor/ha.
HomeLibXps is original MIT code using Windows WPF; its sources and build
script are Utils/HomeLibXps and scripts/prepare-xps-runtime.ps1.
